  "verbalization": "Cornigerine is linked to WI-38 through two distinct pathways, both of which involve the activation of downstream signaling molecules. In the first pathway, Cornigerine targets Vascular endothelial growth factor receptor 2, which is then inhibited by a specific compound, [(Z)-2-...], which in turn targets WI-38. In the second pathway, Cornigerine directly targets Tyrosine-protein kinase SYK, which is inhibited by another compound, 3-Bicyclo[3.2.1]octanyl..., also targeting WI-38. These pathways suggest that Cornigerine may influence WI-38 through the activation or inhibition of key signaling molecules, potentially modulating cellular processes in the cell line. The evidence supports a mechanism where Cornigerine exerts its effects on WI-38 via the regulation of tyrosine kinase signaling or vascular endothelial growth factor receptor 2 signaling, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
